 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass Python body: it reads stdin as bytes, splits into lines, skips the header, takes column 1 as the category and float(column 2) as the value, accumulates per-category sums in a dict, then writes sorted \"cat,sum\" lines formatted with %.2f. It passes the public sample (in-0.txt matches out-0.txt exactly) and is registered as the assayed baseline at 2.048 (noise 3.4%). Two alternative variants (dropping per-line rstrip/empty checks, and a defaultdict version) scored 2.09 and 2.08 against incumbent 2.07, which is within noise, so the body was kept. I'm resting rather than spending more energy on further marginal micro-optimizations.",
