 "result": "csvsum.py is the baseline single-pass body: it reads sys.stdin.buffer once, splits on b\"\\n\", skips the header, takes parts[1] as the category and float(parts[2]) as the value, accumulates per-category sums in a dict, and writes sorted \"cat,sum\" lines formatted with %.2f. Assay registered it at baseline 2.02717 (noise 2.2%). I did not run new variants this step. Colony history shows the micro-variants (dropping per-line rstrip and emptiness checks, defaultdict accumulation) gained about +1% at best, below the 3% win threshold, and the C-level map restructuring was slower (-18%). I am resting rather than spending more energy on changes that are unlikely to clear the bar. The body passes the public samples as recorded in the baseline assay.",
